HTTP 000 means curl got no HTTP answer at all:

18
00:01:19,976 --> 00:01:24,085
nothing listens on port 8081 of your computer.

19
00:01:24,085 --> 00:01:29,891
The container is running; check which of its ports are published:

20
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:35,056
Do not repeat long docker run commands by hand:

21
00:01:35,056 --> 00:01:37,823
let Compose apply the file every time.

22
00:01:39,567 --> 00:01:40,280
Got it.

23
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,031
What do I need to remember?

24
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:50,258
Multi-container applications need networks, names, ports, variables and an order:

25
00:01:50,258 --> 00:01:52,406
easy to get wrong by hand.

26
00:01:52,967 --> 00:01:58,721
Compose describes the application in compose.yaml and manages it as one project.

27
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:04,471
docker compose up -d creates everything; docker compose down removes it.

28
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:10,005
