91
00:05:57,867 --> 00:05:58,436
restart:

92
00:05:58,436 --> 00:06:03,066
unless-stopped restarts crashed containers, not ones you stopped.

93
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,670
Why would I need networking in Compose?

94
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:15,214
Compose creates a network for every project (PROJECT_default) and attaches every service to it.

95
00:06:15,214 --> 00:06:18,815
On that network, each service name is a DNS name:

96
00:06:18,815 --> 00:06:22,710
the API reaches Redis at redis, not at an IP address.

97
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:28,956
You can also declare your own networks and attach each service only where it belongs,

98
00:06:28,956 --> 00:06:33,218
so a front-end component cannot reach the database at all.

