00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,800
What should I know about logs?

258
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:05,093
Docker collects everything a container's main process writes to standard output and standard error.

259
00:18:05,093 --> 00:18:09,940
docker compose logs shows that output for every service of the project,

260
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:14,652
interleaved and prefixed with the container name, or for one service.

261
00:18:14,652 --> 00:18:16,563
The rule that makes it work:

262
00:18:16,563 --> 00:18:21,138
containers log to stdout/stderr, not to files inside the container.

