357
00:24:52,867 --> 00:24:56,876
How does up, down and the project lifecycle work?

358
00:24:57,433 --> 00:24:59,135
up is not only "start":

359
00:24:59,135 --> 00:25:02,464
it converges the running project to the file.

360
00:25:02,464 --> 00:25:10,158
It creates what is missing, recreates containers whose configuration changed, and leaves the rest alone.

361
00:25:10,158 --> 00:25:16,076
stop/start pause and resume containers without removing them; down removes them.

362
00:25:16,076 --> 00:25:18,517
What down removes can be widened:

363
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:26,433
volumes (-v), images (--rmi), and containers of services that are no longer in the file (--remove-orphans).

